ent himself as a  noble hero was pretty cathartic i love  how the creators wrote the scene where  there's a ton of tension and they draw  this out with viserys being deadpan and  slowly approaching daemon you really  don't know where the direction of the  scene is going and it's pretty  surprising that damon had no ill intent  on the surface at least also in this  scene i love the mirroring that they're  doing between otto hightower and  littlefinger him scouring on the side of  the court and staring down people  reminds me heavily of littlefinger and  winterfell which on the subject of otto  hightower rhysafon does so much with so  little dialogue if you think about it  almost all of it is just exposition and  relaying information but yet he's one of  the most engaging characters in the show  so far i think this is due to the fact  of rhysaphon's amazing delivery of every  line that feels meticulously planned and  crafted even him saying a simple line  like your grace has different variations  that's infused with different  connotations what must i say it your  praise your grace your grace your grace  i'm sorry your grace that's hardly how i  viewed it your grace  what you wanted me your great your craze  otto hightower also takes a character  beat between almost every line of  dialogue to thoroughly show us what he's  feeling the scene in which he's relaying  the information of her nearest night out  with damon shows so much hesitation  between each line of dialogue it's  engrossing to see so much conflict with  anim just telling the king information  because otto doesn't know if he should  do the right thing and notify the king  thus angering him or sweep this under  the rug you can even draw from the scene  that otto wanted to tell viserys this  information and is putting on a show of  hesitation but i think the brief shot  before this scene tells the opposite of  this it looks like he's preparing to do  a heinous act like he's going to regret  because otto was 