renier and  damon getting along and so far their  chemistry together is so infectious i  think the contrast of vernier kind of  being unimpressed or not very enthused  by most people's company to them being  with daemon where she's always happy  around him further emphasizes how much  she really likes him and if anyone  thinks their relationship so far is  weird just remember that the targaryens  are very incestuous so honestly that  doesn't bother me at all and this is a  fantasy at the end of the day as long as  they seem like they actually like each  other then the potential romance between  them is a-okay which leads into their  little adventure at night this scene  actually did a lot that i loved firstly  in just one minute of vernier and damon  walking down the street in king's  landing the portrayal of the city feels  so much more real and vibrant than  anything that was shown in the last few  seasons of game of thrones because in  game of thrones king's landing became  extremely shallow and lost all of its  character and just became a mindless  crowd who ironically supported cersei  despite her killing thousands of  innocents  lost was all the grimy characteristics  in the rough edges of the population  however in house of the dragon the  craters show copious amounts of details  and even the placing was a welcomed  edition initially in game of thrones i  didn't really care much for the play  scenes in season 6 because it felt more  like filler but that isn't the case for  this scene because the play shows the  perspective the common people have about  rainier becoming queen right in front of  her it's a lot more relevant than just  recapping the events of the show thus  far in a comedic way but instead  twisting that knife of conflict of  succession into the heart of rhaenyra  then this leads into damon and renera  getting a little frisky which to me the  scene was a little contrived i know  ranira had a bit to drink despite it not  really being clear how drunk she was  which she didn't seem that drunk but she  should be smarter than wanting to have  sex with damon in public because this  event sets forth a lot of major conflict  and any whiff of it not coming across as  natural and was forced to happen by the  writers will feel like it invalidates  the coming scenes i can see why she made  these mistakes because of her alcohol  consumption but i feel like they should  have made that fact more clear that she  was actually under the influence and  wasn't herself because even the scene  after this where she has sex with her  kirsten cole which ay my guy she seems  more sexually frustrated and teased  which drove her to wanting to do that  instead of the alcohol or it's really  just a combination of both  one aspect about the scene though that i  really liked was the contrast between  alison spending her night with visceras  and rainer and damon having a night out  showing love and happiness and then the  opposite side of the coin where it's  more of an obligation and duty that's  becoming taxing there's an overall smart  way to showcase these two scenes  together that perfectly utilizes  parallel editing that and allison in  these scenes is doing a magnificent job  all these young actors so far are really  surprising me like these are genuinely  some outstanding performances  next we have daemon and viserys's  confrontation the blocking of the scene  where daemon is just on the ground as  viserys is looming over him is great it  immediately shows the power dynamic and  viserys is actually being menacing for  once which this episode is showing him  as being more fierce which is nice to  see since he's normally pretty soft in  the scene though it's revealed that  damon was actually making a play for the  throne and lies that he had sex with  renera it turns an already complex  situation and evolves into a surprising  revelation that damon was just  manipulating rainer this whole time his  plan of trying to soil raniera to  devalue her for marriage isn't very  smart because viserys can easily just  deny it and outcast damon but this whole  scenario is still juicy nonetheless  hopefully though this acts as more of a  character building moment for rhaenyra  and her being more resilient to being  manipulated in the future damon's  revelation also offers more context  within the rest of the episode and is  probably why damon was on such good  behavior with his brother earlier i  always love scenes that change the way  you view the prior ones and make you  want to go back and watch them then the  ending of the scene is golden where  daemon after failing just goes to sleep  on the floor because he's hung over i  love that man so much for the final  scene i want to talk about we have  rainer and versailis talk about  potential things that happen in the bump  of the night i like how each episode so  far has a climactic confrontation of  sorts between rainier and viserys this  time though viserys is kind of on his  hot streak of being menacing and he even  kind of scares and unsettles ronira at  the start of the scene he opens the  dialogue with responsibilities that  renewer has inherited and he again  references a song of ice and fire and  talks about the prince who was promised  which going back to the first episode i  don't think they should keep reminding  the audience of the underwhelming end of  game of thrones like ah yes the prince  who was promised is so important that  david and dan completely dropped that  notion all together and just allowed  arya to kill the night king because they  wanted to subvert expectations so the  creators putting the emphasis on this in  house of the dragon is a little  distracting to say the least but the  rest of the scene is obviously great  anything between viserys and or nira is  always stellar and all the conflict they  treach through together is very engaging  overall episode 4 was really good and  initially after finishing it i wasn't  that crazy 